"morBreaker gameplay with a paddle, ball, coloured brick grid, and score display.","https://github.com/KingMordas/mor-breaker","width",1280,"height",720,"credit","GameMap local capture","list","attribution","Creator-attributed clients / models (not inferred from related tools)","items",[80],"Claude Code","links","Related resources",[86,87],"resourceIds","section",{"_57":89,"_25":90},{"_57":80,"_25":88},"/resources/claude-code/","Unity · Manual","/resources/unity-engine/","Creator evidence",[94],"evidence",{"_57":95,"_25":96,"_97":98},"Read the explicit Claude Code contribution breakdown","https://github.com/KingMordas/mor-breaker#built-with-claude-code-","note","Creator disclosure names the Unity MCP package and lists the editor work Claude performed. It is a process summary, not a published prompt transcript.","Source contents","complete project","Project source",[103],{"_57":104,"_25":68,"_97":105},"Open the complete Unity game","MIT-licensed Assets, Packages, ProjectSettings, scenes, and C# gameplay source. Requires Unity 6000.4.11f1; open Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity and press Play. Windows/WebGL build modules are needed only for packaging; Claude/MCP tooling is not required for play.","Access type","download","demo","Play or run",[111],{"_57":112,"_25":113,"_97":114},"Download morBreaker for Windows or WebGL","https://github.com/KingMordas/mor-breaker/releases/tag/v1.2.0","Version 1.2.0 includes Windows standalone and WebGL ZIPs. Extract the Windows build and launch it, or serve the WebGL build over HTTP. A/D or arrows move, Space launches, H shows scores, and Space/Enter restarts. Pointer/touch controls are included; no public hosted play link is supplied.","Game platform","GitHub Releases","Guide format","disclosure","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[122],{"_57":123,"_25":96,"_97":-7},"Read the creator’s Unity and Claude Code account","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[128,129,130,131],"Download the Windows release or serve the published WebGL build 